### A side effect nobody planned

The insurer noticed. When Fruttoria renewed its cargo policy through Seaboard Insurance Brokers on 1 January 2024, the premium came down by 8.5 percent, helped along by a 2023 loss record that no longer needed footnotes. "Our broker actually asked for a copy of the Tidewalk monthly report," says Ewelina. "In nineteen years nobody has asked me for a logistics report voluntarily."

## At a glance

| Fruttoria Baltica | The numbers |
|---|---|
| Customer since | 14 March 2023 |
| Plan | Tidewalk Fairway + KC-Tag 4 |
| Fleet | 410 KC-Tag 4 tags, 2 KC-Hub 200 at Pruszcz Gdański |
| Volume | 1,236 TEU (2023), forecast 1,410 TEU (2024) |
| Excursion alerts per 1,000 container-days | 6.8 (2022) down to 1.9 (H1 2024) |
| Cargo written off | EUR 214,300 (2022) down to EUR 58,900 (2023) |
| Contract renewed | July 2024, 24 months |

## Renewal, and what is next

The contract was renewed in July 2024 for 24 months, with a volume discount that kicks in above a yearly volume Fruttoria passed comfortably. Next on the list is single sign-on: Ewelina's IT department has asked for Tidewalk SSO before the end of November 2024, and Fruttoria has also been pencilled in as one of the first accounts to be invited to the Tidewalk v7 beta in spring 2025. "We are not shy about being the guinea pig," she says, "as long as the guinea pig gets a direct phone number."

Interested in how this would look for your own network? Talk to your Korvane account manager or write to sales@korvane.example. We would love to hear which Monday morning you would like to get rid of.

